{"slug": "odiana", "title": "Odiana", "description": "One head. One law. One canon. One order of temples. The religion of the Igbo, gathered under a single authority — and read here in Ide.", "html": "<main data-page=\"ide:odiana\">\n<article class=\"reader\"><section class=\"section\"><div class=\"site-wrap\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><div><p class=\"eyebrow\">9 DOCUMENTS</p></div><h2 id=\"chapter-0\">Its own documents</h2></div><p class=\"section-description\">Written in Igbo by its own project; shown here in Ide.</p><div class=\"portal-grid\"><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-constitution.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">5,451 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-1\">The constitution</h3><p>The order of the religion: its head, its law, its offices.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-doctrine.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">2,666 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-2\">Doctrine</h3><p>What is taught.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-liturgy.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">3,025 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-3\">Liturgy</h3><p>What is done, and in what order.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-temple.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">2,763 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-4\">The temple</h3><p>The building, and what belongs in it.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-purity.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">3,141 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-5\">Purity</h3><p>Cleanliness as doctrine, not housekeeping.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-afa.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">3,423 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-6\">Afa</h3><p>Divination, and how it is read.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-canon-held.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">2,130 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-7\">The canon</h3><p>What the canon is, and how it is changed.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-home.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">9,034 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-8\">The home</h3><p>The dwelling, how it is arranged and kept.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a><a class=\"portal-tile\" href=\"/odiana-obibi-nso.html\"><div class=\"tile-top\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">46,970 words</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" height=\"14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"14\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div><h3 id=\"chapter-9\">Obibi Nso — the holy book</h3><p>The scripture itself.</p><div class=\"tile-footer\"><span>Read</span><span>→</span></div></a></div></div></section><section class=\"section\"><div class=\"site-wrap\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><h2 id=\"chapter-10\">Odiana and Ide</h2></div><p class=\"section-description\">Ide already carries most of the religion’s own register.</p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>What</th><th>In Igbo</th><th>In Ide</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>the personal force</td><td><code>chi</code></td><td><code>chi</code>, widely said <code>si</code> / <code>sị</code>— <strong>both are Ide</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>the creator</td><td><code>Chukwu</code></td><td><code>Chukwu</code> — the name stands</td></tr>\n<tr><td>the temple</td><td><code>Ndose</code></td><td><code>ndose</code> — Ide’s own word</td></tr>\n<tr><td>the diocese</td><td>—</td><td><code>isiana</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>the bishop</td><td>—</td><td><code>isiafa</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>the king</td><td><code>Igwe</code></td><td><code>ikala</code> — hailed <code>Ezeana</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>the cathedral</td><td>—</td><td><code>obichukwu</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>holiness</td><td><code>nso</code></td><td><code>nso</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>the canon</td><td><code>Obibi Nso</code></td><td><code>òbibi nso</code> — <code>òbibi</code> is Ide for book</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class=\"section\"><div class=\"site-wrap\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><h2 id=\"chapter-11\">Where it stands</h2></div><p><strong>Odiana is a religion of the Igbo, and its own project holds it.</strong> It is written in Igbo — Nri Igbo, Central Igbo and Idemmili Igbo. What is published here is how it reads in the Ide dialect: the terms Ide already carries, and the one term that changes.</p></div></section></article>\n</main>"}